// The fairy ring network: twenty-nine codes, and a ring on the ground for every one of them.
//
// WHY TWENTY-NINE AND NOT FIFTY-FIVE. RuneScape has 55 working codes. A code is only worth having
// if there is a ring at the other end, and thirty of RuneScape's lead to Varlamore, Great
// Kourend, Kebos, the Isle of Souls, Zul-Andra, Grimstone, Yu'biusk and the Abyss: content from
// 2015 to 2025 with no ground on a 2006 map. Three were added in November 2025.
//
// Three more were ruled out by looking rather than guessing, with tools/sim/ringsites.ts:
//
//   DJP  Tower of Life       not on this map. No loc and no npc anywhere matches it.
//   AJS  penguins, Miscellania   Cold War content. There are no penguin locs at all, and the
//                            only Penguin npc on the map is in the Ardougne zoo pen.
//   CKP  cosmic entity plane the plane has no clear 3x3 anywhere on it. A ring needs nine tiles.
//
// EVERY COORDINATE BELOW WAS PROBED, not estimated. Each is walkable, holds no scenery, is joined
// to the mainland, is outdoors by a wall test, fits inside one map square, and has surroundings
// that name the place it claims to be - kalphite_burrow_entrance beside BIQ, npc:Kruk beside CLR,
// mudskipper_sign beside AIQ. That last check is the one that matters: three first drafts were in
// the wrong place entirely, including a "polar hunter area" that landed on Piscatoris next to an
// existing ring, and an "Ardougne Zoo" inside a house with a bath in it.
//
// CLP IS A CORRECTION. This file used to call the ring at (3082, 3206) Port Sarim, give it the
// code AIQ, and state outright that "it is not Draynor island either". That was wrong on both
// counts. A flood fill from that tile reaches 40 tiles and stops: it is an islet, which is
// exactly what RuneScape's CLP is. So it is CLP now, AIQ has gone to the real Mudskipper Point,
// and anyone who learned AIQ in the last week has one letter to relearn. The right-click Zanaris
// option matters most on this one, since the ring is the only way off.
//
// THREE OTHER REALMS THIS MAP DOES HAVE, which the first pass missed by searching the wrong
// field: findmarks.ts read an npc's name in preference to its debugname, so it reported places
// absent that are merely named differently. ALR's abyss sits beside abyss_exit_to_fire and the
// rcu_outer_multi ring, BLP's is among the TzHaar themselves, and BJR's is on the grass outside
// the Fisher King's castle - a first pass put that one in his throne room, among three
// painting2_king and six suits of armour.
//
// DIR's gorak plane was dropped on the same evidence. There is a Gorak npc at (2865, 5262) on
// level 2, but the locs around it are God Wars Dungeon's - gwd_pillar_grapple among them - so
// that is this server's GWD space, not a plane to send anybody to.
//
// ALR IS WORTH A SECOND THOUGHT and is flagged rather than hidden: the abyss is the fast
// runecrafting route, and a fairy ring into it skips the wilderness trip and the Zamorak mage.
// RuneScape does give ALR away with no requirement, so this is authentic rather than generous,
// but it is a real change to how runecrafting is trained here. One line removes it.
//
// TWO MORE FOUND BY LOOKING HARDER, after the npc-name bug above was fixed. Neither answers to
// the name RuneScape uses for it, which is why both read as absent twice:
//
//   DLR  Tirannwn is here under the Regicide quest's own prefix - regicide_tree_fallen,
//        regicide_red_mushroom_fade, regicide_corpse - and nothing in it says isafdar. A first
//        guess of (2200, 3060) landed on High Priestess Zul-Harcinqa instead, which is Zul-Andra.
//   DLS  WAS BUILT AND THEN TAKEN OUT, by choice rather than by error. It was findable: In
//        Search of the Myreque is this server's "route" quest, so a search for /myreque/ finds
//        nothing, but freedomfighterentrance sits beside hollowtree_entrance at (3509, 3447),
//        which IS The Hollows, and Veliaf Hurtz stands at (3505, 9838) in the cave below. The
//        reason it is gone is that these rings are gated on Fairytale Part I alone, so the ring
//        let a player who had never met the Myreque walk into their hideout. RuneScape gates DLS
//        on In Search of the Myreque instead, which this world has no varp to check here. If that
//        gate ever exists, 55_fairy_mushroom_ring is still in the cache and (3500, 9810) is a
//        probed, boundary-safe spot two tiles from the hideout door.
//
// AIR AND BIP STAY UNBUILT, and the reason is worth keeping so nobody repeats the search. Both
// are empty islands with no landmark to find, so they were looked for geometrically instead - and
// the islands that exist are the wrong ones. South-east of Ardougne there is the Fishing Trawler
// dock (game_trawler_reward_net, winch, anchor) and a 138-tile island of moss giants; on the
// Salve the only island with room on it is the Nature Spirit's grotto. Putting a ring on any of
// those and calling it AIR or BIP would be the Port Sarim mistake over again.
//
// A CODE IS JUST THE VARP, and it is worth saying why rather than how. The first version of this
// had two encodings for one thing: %fairy_ring_dial packs dial 1 into the LOW bits, while the
// lookup key was written dial1 * 16 + dial2 * 4 + dial3, weighting dial 1 highest. Both are
// defensible and they disagree - 26 is DKR read one way and CKS read the other - so a test that
// set the varp directly dialled a dead code while believing it had dialled Edgeville, and a
// deliberately broken quest gate went unnoticed because the teleport it should have let through
// was never reachable in the first place.
//
// So there is one encoding: the code IS the six bits, dial1 + dial2 * 4 + dial3 * 16, read
// straight out of the varp. Each dial is 0-3 in the order the dial turns (A D C B / I L K J /
// P S R Q - see fairy_rings.enum). 64 possible codes, 29 of them real; the rest are a ring that
// hums and does nothing, which is what RuneScape does with an unused code too. AIP is 0, so a
// player who has never touched the dial opens it on a code that goes nowhere.

^fairy_code_aiq = 48  // Mudskipper Point
^fairy_code_ajr = 44  // slayer cave SE of Rellekka
^fairy_code_akq = 56  // Piscatoris
^fairy_code_aks = 24  // Feldip hunter area
^fairy_code_alp = 4   // the Lighthouse
^fairy_code_alq = 52  // the Haunted Woods
^fairy_code_alr = 36  // the Abyssal Area
^fairy_code_als = 20  // McGrubor's Wood
^fairy_code_biq = 51  // the Kalphite Hive
^fairy_code_bis = 19  // Ardougne, by the zoo
^fairy_code_bjr = 47  // the Fisher King's realm
^fairy_code_bkp = 11  // Chompy marsh
^fairy_code_bkr = 43  // Mort Myre
^fairy_code_bks = 27  // Zanaris
^fairy_code_blp = 7   // the TzHaar city
^fairy_code_blr = 39  // the Legends' Guild
^fairy_code_cip = 2   // Miscellania
^fairy_code_ciq = 50  // north-west of Yanille
^fairy_code_cjr = 46  // Sinclair Mansion (east)
^fairy_code_ckr = 42  // south of Tai Bwo Wannai
^fairy_code_cks = 26  // Canifis
^fairy_code_clp = 6   // Draynor island
^fairy_code_clr = 38  // Ape Atoll
^fairy_code_dis = 17  // the Wizards' Tower
^fairy_code_dkp = 9   // the Karamja gnome glider
^fairy_code_dkr = 41  // Edgeville
^fairy_code_dks = 25  // the polar hunter area
^fairy_code_dlq = 53  // north of Nardah
^fairy_code_dlr = 37  // Isafdar, in Tirannwn

// Where each code puts you: the centre tile of the ring at the far end.
^fairy_to_mudskipper    = 0_46_48_51_41    // 2995, 3113
^fairy_to_trollcave     = 0_43_56_28_30    // 2780, 3614
^fairy_to_piscatoris    = 0_36_56_15_35    // 2319, 3619
^fairy_to_feldip        = 0_39_45_60_44    // 2556, 2924
^fairy_to_lighthouse    = 0_39_56_9_50     // 2505, 3634
^fairy_to_hauntedwoods  = 0_56_55_16_3     // 3600, 3523
^fairy_to_mcgrubor      = 0_41_54_20_39    // 2644, 3495
^fairy_to_kalphite      = 0_50_48_30_34    // 3230, 3106
^fairy_to_ardougnezoo   = 0_40_51_36_13    // 2596, 3277
^fairy_to_chompy        = 0_37_47_25_37    // 2393, 3045
^fairy_to_mortmyre      = 0_54_53_14_38    // 3470, 3430
^fairy_to_zanaris       = 0_37_69_44_18    // 2412, 4434
^fairy_to_legends       = 0_42_52_45_25    // 2733, 3353
^fairy_to_miscellania   = 0_39_60_15_46    // 2511, 3886
^fairy_to_yanille       = 0_39_48_25_55    // 2521, 3127
^fairy_to_sinclair      = 0_42_55_17_56    // 2705, 3576
^fairy_to_taibwo        = 0_43_47_45_1     // 2797, 3009
^fairy_to_canifis       = 0_53_54_55_14    // 3447, 3470
^fairy_to_draynorisland = 0_48_50_10_6     // 3082, 3206
^fairy_to_apeatoll      = 0_42_43_24_33    // 2712, 2785
^fairy_to_wiztower      = 0_48_49_36_13    // 3108, 3149
^fairy_to_karamjaglider = 0_46_46_26_34    // 2970, 2978
^fairy_to_edgeville     = 0_48_54_57_40    // 3129, 3496
^fairy_to_polar         = 0_42_59_18_1     // 2706, 3777
^fairy_to_nardah        = 0_53_46_22_61    // 3414, 3005
^fairy_to_abyss         = 0_47_75_17_33    // 3025, 4833
^fairy_to_tzhaar        = 0_38_80_8_26     // 2440, 5146
^fairy_to_fisherking    = 0_41_73_5_5      // 2629, 4677
^fairy_to_isafdar       = 0_34_48_24_48    // 2200, 3120

// The Lumbridge Swamp shed, which the Zanaris ring by Fairy Nuff has always stepped out to. Kept
// as a second option on that one ring rather than replaced by the dial - it is a route players
// already use, and taking it away to add a feature would be a poor trade.
^fairy_to_swamp = 0_50_49_1_33         // 3201, 3169

// Bit positions in %fairy_ring_dial. Two bits per dial.
^fairy_dial1_lo = 0
^fairy_dial1_hi = 1
^fairy_dial2_lo = 2
^fairy_dial2_hi = 3
^fairy_dial3_lo = 4
^fairy_dial3_hi = 5
